<div id="outline-container-5" class="outline-2">
<h2 id="5">New release of Merlin and OCaml LSP</h2>
<div class="outline-text-2" id="text-5">
<p>
Archive: <a href="https://discuss.ocaml.org/t/ann-new-release-of-merlin-ocaml-lsp/18846/1">https://discuss.ocaml.org/t/ann-new-release-of-merlin-ocaml-lsp/18846/1</a>
</p>
</div>
<div id="outline-container-orgbdc092d" class="outline-3">
<h3 id="orgbdc092d">Tim ats announced</h3>
<div class="outline-text-3" id="text-orgbdc092d">
<p>
I am very pleased to announce new releases of Merlin and OCaml LSP for OCaml 5.5.
</p>

<p>
Merlin release features some bug fixes and improvements for some commands:
</p>
<ul class="org-ul">
<li><code>destruct</code> should now work on let-binding patterns, allowing you to expand a wildcard in snippets of the form <code>let _ = ... in</code></li>
<li><code>selection-range</code> command has been reworked in order to produce more intuitive results.</li>
<li><code>ocaml-index</code> file should now be more compact to store, and the project index should be built more quickly thanks to changes in its file format</li>
</ul>

<p>
Some known bugs were also fixed:
</p>
<ul class="org-ul">
<li>Fix a caching issue making inconsistent compilation units stale</li>
<li>Ghost bindings should not be printed in the editor's outline</li>
<li>Fix a regression introduced by the recent improvement made in ocaml-index file handling</li>
</ul>

<p>
OCaml LSP releases include numerous improvements and bug fixes, thanks to @rgrinberg's contributions.
</p>

<p>
<b>Complete changelogs:</b>
</p>
<ul class="org-ul">
<li><a href="https://github.com/ocaml/merlin/blob/main/CHANGES.md?plain=1#L8">Merlin 5.9.1</a></li>
<li><a href="https://github.com/ocaml/ocaml-lsp/blob/master/CHANGES.md?plain=1#L1">OCaml LSP 1.28.1</a></li>
</ul>

<p>
cc @vds @xvw @lyrm @panglesd @PizieDust
</p>
</div>
