</div>
<div id="outline-container-orga01fd98" class="outline-3">
<h3 id="orga01fd98">Jon Sterling announced</h3>
<div class="outline-text-3" id="text-orga01fd98">
<p>
Dear OCaml community,
</p>

<p>
I'm really happy to be able to announce the release of Forester 6.0 (<code>forester</code>) on opam. This is a huge quality-of-life release with many improvements, but no (intentional) language changes. See the <a href="https://www.forester-notes.org/VNQB/">release notes</a> for details.
</p>

<p>
<b>A few highlights:</b>
</p>

<ol class="org-ol">
<li>HTML is emitted instead of XML by default, but users who prefer the XML output can still get it using <code>--emit-xml</code>. The reason for this change is that the major browser vendors have colluded to remove XSLT from the web platform, which has made Forester's prior design untenable as a default. We don't have any plans to remove XML support.</li>
<li>Forester now ships bundled with a default "theme". If you are happy with the default output, then there is no need to have a <code>theme</code> directory in your forest anymore.</li>
<li>Forester 6.0 is several times faster than Forester 5.0. This is due to our adoption of multicore OCaml.</li>
<li>When the language server is connected, it automatically fires up a live preview server at <code>localhost:8080</code>. The preview updates live while you are typing into your editor. Currently file watching is not supported, so only edits that pass through the LSP are reflected; this limitation will be lifted in a future release.</li>
</ol>

<p>
This release is due primarily to the hard work of @kentookura over the past year, and it would not have been possible without the generous support of <b>Tarides</b> and the <b>OCaml Software Foundation</b>. I'm incredibly grateful for all the support.
</p>

<p>
Best,
Jon
</p>
